    "q-74051": {
      "dom_id": "step-q74051",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Suppose $(a+b)\\cdot a=0$, where $a\\ne 0.$ Which of the following statements are true? \n\nI. $a\\cdot a=0$\n\nII. $a\\cdot b>0$\n\nIII. $a\\cdot b<0$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Since $a\\ne 0$, we must have $a\\cdot a>0.$\n\n- Statement II is false while statement III is true. Simplifying the expression $(a+b)\\cdot a=0$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(a+b)\\cdot a & =0 \\\\ a\\cdot a+b\\cdot a & =0 \\\\ a\\cdot a+a\\cdot b & =0 \\\\ a\\cdot b & =-a\\cdot a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nSince $a\\ne 0$ implies that $a\\cdot a>0$, we obtain that $-a\\cdot a<0.$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the correct answer is \"III only\".",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
